Description:
Overview:

Effectively manage operational aspects of the spa and retail to include adequate staffing levels, complete financial management’s duties including: budgeting, forecasting, payroll and scheduling, as well as product inventory and ordering, establishing and maintaining high level of customer service based on Napa First Street guiding principles and culture. Oversee Spa Manager, Spa Supervisor, Massage Therapists, Estheticians and Nail Technicians ensuring proper techniques and service standards are met. Work closely with Resort Sales and Conference Services in an effort to maximize spa services and retail sales to all resort and group guests.


Responsibilities:

* Full operational responsibility of the daily operations of the Spa and reatil operations;
* Inventory of professional and reatil products managed to capture full revenue potentials;
* Interview and select excellent staff to create a leading service and treatment presentation;
* Direct, train and maintain high level of job satisfaction/morale/teamwork among associates in respective areas of responsibility;
* Responsible for performance evaluations and disciplinary procedures;
* Create and follow all financial planning, budgets and payroll;
* Responsible for reviewing daily forecasts and budget and managing expenses as well as reviewing daily sales to be sure controls/systems are in place to ensure accuracy;
* Oversee management of professional inventory to include ordering, receiving and inventory in conjunction with Account Manager and Lead Therapist;
* Attend weekly manager meetings;
* Executes HRAF’s and discussion documentation;
* Updates daily associate punch edit sheets;
* Assist in ensuring cleanliness of public spa areas to include spa retail, treatment rooms, storage areas and product storage;
* Responsible for coordination and execution of spa packages;
* Scheduling of various services for individuals and large groups;
* Implement strategic and tactical plans to achieve departmental financial budgeting goals and expectations;
* Consistently deliver accurate forecasting projections for areas of responsibility and implement effective adjustments as required in staffing and other cost drivers to ensure margin integrity;
* Coordinates all immediate staff meetings;
* Primary contact for all Group business and sales activity;
* Attend group pre-con meetings as requested;
* Coordinates and executes group activity including booking spa appointments, follow-up with group contact, and billing;
* Create, manage and update procedure manuals for all operation aspects of the spa;
* Develop and implement operational policies and procedures to include: Basic Spa Procedures and Protocols; Product Requisitions; Safety Procedures; Schedule Change Protocol; Employee Procedures, etc;
* Coordinates and oversees training opportunities regarding new associates on both services and retail product lines;
* Coordinate and standardize all rules and regulations regarding coordinators, massage therapists, nail technicians and estheticians;
* Work with Assistant General Manager and other leadership in determining marketing strategies based on sales activity;
* Consistently researches and recommends change in retail and professional products, keeping abreast of market and industry trends/changes;
* Participates in updating and creating Spa menu;
* Promotes and champions resort culture and guiding principles, leads this process on an ongoing basis;
* Assists in conducting monthly trend statistics on treatments and peak operating times;
* Ensures that associates meet all department dress & grooming standards;
* Provide continual direction and training regarding standards for guest service, treatment rooms and product knowledge;
* Act as liaison between internal and external departments;
* Other duties as assigned;

Qualifications:

* Minimum of 3-5 years experience in Spa and reatil operations or related field;
* prefer opening experience
* familiar with Forbes ratings and standards
* Minimum of 2 year experience in customer service and sales;
* Must have working knowledge of computer programs: Word, Excel and Microsoft Outlook;
* Must have High School Diploma;
* Retail purchasing and inventory knowledge;
* Prefer experience with revenue and expense management;
* Strong customer service orientation/member and guest relation’s skills;
* Attention to detail and high standards of quality and cleanliness;
* Excellent analytical and problem solving skills;
* Interpersonal, communication and listening skills – with both external and internal customers.
* Prefer knowledge of POS/Booking Software
* Must have a working understanding of Resort culture and vision
* Must be able to handle pressure situations with ease

**As a valued member of the CoralTree team, you'll receive a comprehensive benefits package that includes:**

* Group medical, dental, vision, life, and disability benefits
* Participation in a pre-tax flexible benefit plan for healthcare and dependent care reimbursement
* An employee assistance program
* Paid time off/sick time
* Participation in a 401(k) plan with a company match

Join us in creating unforgettable experiences for our guests, building vibrant communities, and shaping the future of travel and hospitality.
